w: Girls and boys come | out to play, The | moon doth shine _ as | bright as day; | Leave your sup-per, and | leave your sleep; | Come to your play-fel-lows | in the street; | Come with a whoop, and | come with a call, Come | with a good will _ or | not at all. | Up the lad-der and | down _ the wall, A | pen-ny _ loaf _ will | serve you all.
